    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated offensive profile, anchored by **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas**. **Sam Antonacci** is our strongest play today, boasting a 47.20 efficiency score despite a difficult matchup against Williams, G. His lead-off status in the batting order (+10%) and a favorable platoon advantage (+7%) sustain his value, effectively neutralizing the impact of an elite opposing SP_xERA of 2.95. While **Miguel Vargas** also draws the same pitcher, his output is more heavily suppressed by the SP skill factor (-19%), resulting in a marginal 40.41 score. We are relying on **Sam Antonacci** to catalyze the top of the lineup; his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in a category-starved 5x5 environment.\n\nThe decision to bench **Brayan Rocchio** was the most difficult call of the morning. With a score of 38.59, he fell just shy of our 40.0 floor threshold. The primary detriments were his #9 spot in the batting order (-8%) and the sustained SP skill of Burke, S (3.79), which stifled his offensive ceiling. We have elected to keep **Brayan Rocchio** on the pine to protect our daily game caps rather than risking a sub-par performance against a tough right-handed arm. Elsewhere, the bench remains heavy with inactive assets, as **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are sidelined due to team off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains unavailable on the IL. We will monitor lineup changes for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Heliot Ramos** closely, as the absence of confirmed data for some roster pieces adds a layer of volatility to our current projections.",
